hypothesis: 'Every version from v021 has trained with state_reset=2000 and served
  with 4000, an accidental skew nobody intended. Measuring it showed serving at 4000
  beats serving at 2000 by +0.001221, which is 7.7 sigma and the largest single effect
  we have measured in months. That raises a sharp question: is the gain from the LONGER
  horizon at serving, or from the train/serve MISMATCH? v042 is the mismatch arm and
  v047 is the matched arm at the same 4000 interval. If matched wins, the mismatch
  was luck and should be closed. If matched loses, the mismatch is a real effect worth
  keeping and pushing further (v048).'
